  "worked_solution": "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\frac{\\pi }{2}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{sin}\u20613x-\\operatorname{cos}\u20613x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{sin}\u20613x-\\operatorname{cos}\u20613x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}\u20613x-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}\u20613x)|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\pi }[(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}))-(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2}))+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2})))] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\pi }[(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))-(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\pi }[(0+(-1))-(0+1)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\pi }(-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
